Waterloo MCP server

This package exposes read-only access to Waterloo data roots over MCP.

Current v1 focus:
- list configured roots
- inspect the indexed Waterloo data behind them
- keep the server simple and stdio-based for local development
- offer Streamable HTTP for Inspector-based inspection at `/mcp`

The current entry point is `wtrl_mcp`.
The Inspector-friendly entry point is `sdv.doc.waterloo.mcp.server:app`.

Typical usage:
- start the server with one or more roots
- use `--transport stdio` for a local child-process integration
- use `--transport streamable-http` for the browser Inspector
- set `WTRL_MCP_ALLOWED_ORIGINS` for browser-origin allowlisting, as a
  comma-separated list
- set `WTRL_MCP_ALLOWED_HOSTS` if the HTTP Host header needs allowlisting, as a
  comma-separated list
- browser Inspector example:
  - `WTRL_MCP_ROOTS=package_main/src/sdv/doc/waterloo`
  - `WTRL_MCP_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://gilgamesh:6274`
  - `WTRL_MCP_ALLOWED_HOSTS=127.0.0.1:8000`
  - `wtrl_mcp --transport streamable-http package_main/src/sdv/doc/waterloo`
- connect the Inspector to `http://127.0.0.1:8000/mcp`
- inspect `tools/list`
- call `list_docs`

The server is intentionally read-only in v1.
